:: Inklink [config]
kind: story-game
tags: mystery ~ whodunit ~ time travel ~ train
ages: 12..
mode: cohort
cohort: 2..=5 ~ best 3..=4
clock: 0..=5 ~ shown as "stop" ~ advance consensus ~ turn limit 24h
start: lounge@0
default clash: random_winner
default moves: walk, dash

place sleeper: "the sleeper car"
place dining: "the dining car"
place lounge: "the observation lounge"
place baggage: "the baggage car"
place mail: "the mail car"
place platform: "the station platform" ~ offstage
route: sleeper - dining - lounge - baggage - mail ~ shown as "car"
way vestibule: baggage - platform
~ one way
~ for npc
~ open when clock.now >= 1
~ loud
~ shown as "the vestibule door"

resource vults: 3 ~ refill each chronon ~ shown as "minutes"
resource rewinds: 2 ~ max 3 ~ shown as "charges"

act walk: cost 2 ~ steps 1 ~ ends turn
act dash: requires full vults ~ cost 1 per step ~ steps 1..=2 ~ ends turn ~ loud
act slip: cost 3 ~ steps 1 ~ ends turn ~ quiet
act observe: cost rest ~ min 1 ~ ends turn
act take: cost 1 ~ shared ~ capacity 1
act force: cost 2 ~ shared ~ capacity 1 ~ loud
act examine: cost 1 ~ private
act ask: cost 1 ~ private
act confront: cost 1 ~ shared ~ capacity many
act wind: cost rest ~ min 1 ~ private ~ ends turn

item compartment_key: "a brass key on a fob stamped S.A." ~ held by wren
item letter: "Mrs. Ardent’s letter" ~ evidence ~ motive ~ held by ardent
item vial: "Mrs. Ardent’s vial" ~ evidence ~ held by ardent

clue scorched_wrist: "A thin, glassy burn rings the Professor’s wrist, exactly where the chronometer’s strap sat."
clue burn_pattern: "A burn like that comes from a discharge inside a device, not from touching a live wire." ~ proof_how
clue bruise: "The bruise on his temple came after his heart stopped. He didn’t die from the fall." ~ clears
clue two_hands: "The patent blueprint is annotated in two hands: his blocky capitals, and a smaller slanted script correcting him, initialed E." ~ motive
clue wet_shoes: "Miss Vell “sleeps” with her shoes on, soaked to the laces, though she swears she never left her berth." ~ proof_who
clue debts: "The Professor owed a fortune to Mr. Crane’s client. Tonight’s sale was to pay it." ~ motive
clue saw_vell: "Miss Vell slipped out of the lounge, toward the dining car, a moment before the lights died." ~ proof_who
clue crane_bailiff: "“I’m no buyer. I’m a bailiff. That model is collateral, and I was at this bar all night. Ask anyone.”" ~ clears
clue hobbs_napkin: "“When the lights went, Miss Vell was in my car, wrapping her hand in one of my napkins. She went back the moment they came on.”" ~ proof_who
clue coldwater_step: "At Coldwater a woman stepped off the front of the train into the rain, bent over the rain barrel, and climbed back aboard." ~ proof_who
clue duplicate_filing: "Telegram from the Patent Office: “APPLICATION CONFLICTS WITH PRIOR FILING IN NAME OF E. VELL. ADVISE.”" ~ motive
clue laudanum: "Mrs. Ardent’s vial holds laudanum: a sleeping draught, far too weak to kill." ~ clears
clue the_attack: "In the dark: small hands, black with soot, and the smell of machine oil. Then your watch fired." ~ proof_who

fact wound_watch: no ~ belongs to character

fuse nerve: 3 ~ shown as "Miss Vell’s nerve" ~ hidden
~ then set vell.cornered: yes

character ada: "Ada Thorne, financier" ~ investor ~ playable ~ else absent ~ knows debts
character rook: "Captain Hal Rook, retired" ~ investor ~ playable ~ else absent ~ moves walk ~ knows saw_vell
character wren: "Wren Hollis, investor" ~ investor ~ playable ~ else absent ~ moves walk, dash, slip
character sallow: "Dr. Imogen Sallow, physician" ~ investor ~ playable ~ else absent ~ knows burn_pattern
character guest: "a guest of your own" ~ investor ~ playable ~ custom ~ else absent

npc vell: "Miss Edith Vell" ~ suspect ~ moves walk, dash
npc crane: "Mr. Crane" ~ suspect ~ moves none
npc ardent: "Mrs. Cora Ardent" ~ suspect ~ moves none ~ in dining
npc hobbs: "Hobbs, the steward" ~ witness ~ moves none ~ in dining
npc marsh: "Colonel Marsh" ~ witness ~ moves none ~ in sleeper
~ asleep during 2..=4
~ wakes on loud
~ stays awake 1

scenario night_one:
~ culprit vell
~ method device
~ methods device, poison, fall

objective proof: "Find evidence that names the killer"
~ done when count(evidence, held_by: cohort) >= 1

:: vell [npc]
fact cornered: no
fact shoes_seen: no
fact shown_cufflink: no
fact exposed: no
let target: self.last_seen(holding: evidence)
let blocker: one(linker, in: here)
let bonus: 0
let bonus: 1 when blocker.is(rook)
--
starts: lounge@0
ties: first

goal flee:
~ toward platform
~ weight 6
~ pace dash
~ when self.cornered

goal silence:
~ toward target
~ weight 5
~ then teach target the_attack when alone_with(self, target)
~ then kill target when alone_with(self, target)

goal burn_notebook:
~ toward sleeper
~ weight 4
~ when notebook.exists and not notebook.secured
~ then destroy notebook

goal lie_low:
~ toward sleeper
~ weight 3
~ when clock.now in 2..=4
~ then feign sleep

goal guard_model:
~ toward mail
~ weight 2

reaction chase:
~ when self.saw(dash, toward: self.heading)
~ then dash toward self.heading

reaction surrender:
~ when self.leaving and count(linker, in: here) >= 2
~ then detain vell

reaction standoff:
~ when self.leaving and count(linker, in: here) == 1
~ then roll standoff

table standoff: roll d6 + bonus
~ 1..=2: then teach blocker the_attack
~ 1..=2: then kill blocker
~ 3..=4: nothing
~ 5..: then detain vell

:: cast [lobby]
Five passengers boarded with invitations to the Professor’s demonstration. Who are you tonight?
> [[Ada Thorne->dossier]] ~ become ada
> [[Captain Rook->dossier]] ~ become rook
> [[Wren Hollis->dossier]] ~ become wren
> [[Dr. Imogen Sallow->dossier]] ~ become sallow
> [[Someone else->naming]] ~ become guest

:: naming [lobby]
What name is on your ticket?

{name input for: me.name, max: 24}
> [[Board the train->dossier]] ~ when me.name != ""

:: dossier [lobby]
[if me.is(ada)]
Ada Thorne, of Thorne & Gage. You fund inventions, and you are rarely wrong. The Professor invited you to buy a stake tonight.

[if me.is(ada)]
For your eyes only: last month the Professor begged your bank for a loan to pay his debts. You refused. If tonight’s sale had failed, you meant to buy the patent cheaply yourself.

[if me.is(rook)]
Captain Hal Rook. You came because Colonel Marsh insisted, and because the bar on the night express is excellent.

[if me.is(rook)]
For your eyes only: in the dark you saw Miss Vell slip out of the lounge just before the lights died. A gentleman doesn’t accuse a lady without proof.

[if me.is(wren)]
Wren Hollis, who made a fortune in timepieces and never asks anyone where theirs came from.

[if me.is(wren)]
For your eyes only: at dinner you lifted a brass key from the Professor’s pocket. It opens his compartment in the sleeper.

[if me.is(sallow)]
Dr. Imogen Sallow, the Professor’s physician. You came as an investor and, he joked, in case anything went wrong.

[if me.is(sallow)]
For your eyes only: last week he asked you whether a strong current could stop a weak heart. You told him yes.

[if me.is(guest)]
{me.name}. Nobody quite remembers inviting you. That is useful.

[note]
Paper only for now: the Guest’s gift, one true yes-or-no question about where a passenger was. A digital version could be a single Inquest.

[end]
> [[Board the train->lounge@0]]

:: sleeper [place]
--
item notebook: "the Professor’s notebook" ~ evidence ~ proof_how ~ motive

:: dining [place]
--
item cufflink: "a scorched cufflink, monogrammed E.V." ~ evidence ~ proof_who ~ proof_how

:: lounge [place]
--
item vell_ticket: "Miss Vell’s ticket, never punched" ~ evidence ~ proof_who

:: mail [place]
--
item patent_model: "the patent model" ~ evidence ~ motive

:: the_body [lib]
> [[Examine the body->the_body:examine]] ~ examine

:: the_body:examine [act]
learn scorched_wrist
learn bruise when me.is(sallow)
--
A thin, glassy burn rings his wrist, exactly where the chronometer’s strap sat.

[if me.is(sallow); append]
And the bruise at his temple is wrong: it came after his heart had already stopped.

:: lounge_bar [lib]
> [[Question Mr. Crane->lounge_bar:crane]] ~ ask ~ cost 0 when me.is(ada)

:: lounge_bar:crane [act]
learn crane_bailiff when me.knows.debts
--
[if clock.now == 0]
“I was at the bar, as everyone saw.” He turns his glass a quarter turn.

[else]
“Dreadful business. I was at this bar the whole time.”

[if me.knows.debts]
You mention the money. He sets the glass down. “Very well. I’m no buyer. I’m a bailiff, and that model is collateral.”

:: compartment [lib]
> [[Unlock the Professor’s compartment->compartment:unlock]]
~ take notebook
~ when me.holds.compartment_key
> [[Force the Professor’s compartment->compartment:force]]
~ force
~ when notebook.exists and not me.holds.compartment_key
~ then gain notebook when attempt.success

:: compartment:unlock [act]
[if attempt.success]
The key turns without a sound.

{embed nib: 'notebook_page'}

[else]
{claimants} got there first.

:: compartment:force [act]
[if attempt.success]
The lock gives with a crack that wakes the whole car.

{embed nib: 'notebook_page'}

[else]
{claimants} got there first.

:: notebook_page [lib]
On the desk lies his notebook. The last entry: “Sign with Crane’s man tonight. E. must not know.” Beside a sketch of the master chronometer: “Never wind past the red mark. The coil will discharge.”

:: colonel [lib]
> [[Talk with the Colonel->colonel:talk]] ~ ask ~ when not here.asleep(marsh)
> [[Wake the Colonel->colonel:wake]] ~ ask ~ for rook ~ when here.asleep(marsh)

:: colonel:talk [act]
learn coldwater_step when clock.now >= 3
--
[if clock.now <= 1]
“Ardent? Brilliant fellow. Couldn’t mend a pocket watch to save his life, mind. Had a girl in the workshop for that.”

[if clock.now == 2]
“Can’t a man sleep on this train?”

[if clock.now >= 3]
“At Coldwater someone stepped off into the rain and back on. Light step. A woman’s.”

:: colonel:wake [act]
wake marsh
learn coldwater_step when clock.now >= 3
--
[if clock.now == 2]
“Let a man sleep, Rook. Ask me after Merrow.”

[else]
He grumbles awake. “At Coldwater, Rook. Someone stepped off into the rain and back on.”

:: berth [lib]
> [[Look closer at Miss Vell->berth:shoes]] ~ examine ~ when here.asleep(vell)

:: berth:shoes [act]
let stirs: roll d6
learn wet_shoes
burn nerve 1 when not vell.shoes_seen
set vell.shoes_seen: yes
--
Her shoes are soaked to the laces, though she swears she never left her berth.

[if stirs == 6; append]
Her eyelids flicker. She isn’t asleep.

:: dining_table [lib]
> [[Unroll the blueprint->dining_table:blueprint]] ~ examine
> [[Pocket the glint->dining_table:cufflink]] ~ take cufflink
> [[Ask Hobbs about the blackout->dining_table:hobbs]] ~ ask
> [[Ask Mrs. Ardent about her letter->dining_table:letter]]
~ ask
~ cost 2 when me.is(rook)
~ hidden until me.knows.two_hands
> [[Ask what she gave him->dining_table:vial]] ~ ask
> [[Lift her letter->dining_table:lift_letter]] ~ take letter ~ for wren
> [[Lift her vial->dining_table:lift_vial]] ~ take vial ~ for wren

:: dining_table:blueprint [act]
learn two_hands
--
The patent drawings for the watch. Every margin carries two hands: his blocky capitals, and a smaller slanted script correcting him.

{reveal link: 'Look closer at the slanted script', text: 'The corrections are initialed “E.”'}

:: dining_table:cufflink [act]
[if attempt.success]
A silver cufflink, monogrammed E.V. The enamel is crazed and cracked, as if by a sudden heat.

[else]
Your fingers close on nothing.

[if attempt.clashed; append]
{claimants} reached for it at the same moment.

:: dining_table:hobbs [act]
learn hobbs_napkin
--
Hobbs lowers his voice. “When the lights went, Miss Vell was in my car, wrapping her hand in one of my napkins. She went back the moment they came on.”

:: dining_table:letter [act]
“It is for my solicitor, and none of your concern.” Her eyes stay on the blueprint.

:: dining_table:vial [act]
learn laudanum when me.is(sallow)
--
She sets a small brown vial on the cloth, half full. “My sleeping draught. Satisfied?”

[if me.is(sallow)]
You know the label, and the dose: laudanum, far too weak to kill.

:: dining_table:lift_letter [act]
[if attempt.success]
The letter is in your sleeve before her hand comes back. Old habits. “To my solicitor: begin the divorce. I cannot stay married to a man who steals another’s life’s work.”

[else]
She lays two fingers on the letter without looking at you.

:: dining_table:lift_vial [act]
[if attempt.success]
The vial is in your sleeve before she misses it. Old habits.

[else]
She moves her handbag to her lap without looking at you.

:: ticket [lib]
> [[Pick up the ticket stub->ticket:take]] ~ take vell_ticket

:: ticket:take [act]
burn nerve 1 when attempt.success
--
[if attempt.success]
Miss Vell’s ticket, never punched. It must have been under him since the lights went out.

[else]
{claimants} got to it first.

:: baggage_car [lib]
let can_wind: me.rewinds < 3 and not me.wound_watch
--
> [[Wind your watch at the generator->baggage_car:wind]] ~ wind ~ when can_wind
> [[Look at the vestibule door->baggage_car:door]] ~ examine

:: baggage_car:wind [act]
raise rewinds 1
set me.wound_watch: yes
--
The hum climbs into your teeth, then into your watch, then settles. One more charge.

:: baggage_car:door [act]
A small handprint in soot on the handle, fresh. Someone has tried this door tonight.

:: crate [lib]
> [[Pry open the crate->crate:pry]] ~ take patent_model ~ cost 2

:: crate:pry [act]
[if attempt.success]
A brass-and-glass chronometer in a case addressed to the Patent Office: “Inventor: S. Ardent.” Under the mainspring, engraved very small: E.

[else]
Another pair of hands lifts the model out first.

:: telegram [lib]
> [[Read the telegram->telegram:read]] ~ examine

:: telegram:read [act]
learn duplicate_filing
--
From the Patent Office: “APPLICATION CONFLICTS WITH PRIOR FILING IN NAME OF E. VELL. ADVISE.”

:: pressure [lib]
> [[Show Miss Vell the scorched cufflink->pressure:cufflink]]
~ confront
~ when here.has(vell) and me.holds.cufflink and not vell.shown_cufflink
> [[Say aloud what her ticket and her shoes mean->pressure:aloud]]
~ confront
~ when me.holds.vell_ticket and me.knows.wet_shoes and not vell.exposed

:: pressure:cufflink [act]
burn nerve 1
set vell.shown_cufflink: yes
--
You hold it up. Miss Vell goes very still, and then she smiles, too quickly.

:: pressure:aloud [act]
burn nerve 2
set vell.exposed: yes
--
You lay it out for everyone here: her ticket under the body, her shoes wet from Coldwater. By the next stop, the whole train has heard.

:: lounge@0 [prologue card:01]
Midnight. In the observation lounge, Professor Silas Ardent lifts a brass chronometer toward the lamps. “Ladies, gentlemen: time, made portable.” He winds it once, twice—

[after 2s; append]
The lights die.

[after 4s]
When they return, the Professor lies across the demonstration table. Each of you still wears one of his prototypes, ticking.

{sound effect: 'brakes'}

[if me.knows.saw_vell]
In the dark you are sure of one thing: Miss Vell slipped out a moment before.

[if me.knows.debts]
You know what the papers don’t: he owed Mr. Crane’s client a fortune.

[if me.knows.burn_pattern]
You have seen burns like his before, on men who stood too close to machines.

[end]
Mr. Crane hasn’t moved from the bar. Miss Vell hurries in from the dining car as the lights return. {present} are here. The first stop is close; decide together who goes where.

[note]
Planning beat: chat is open, and nobody commits a move until everyone is ready.

[end]
{embed nib: 'the_body'}
{embed nib: 'lounge_bar'}
> [[Question Miss Vell->lounge@0:vell]] ~ ask ~ cost 2 when me.is(rook)

:: lounge@0:vell [act]
“I went to fetch his spare coil. I came back and—oh, God.” Her right hand stays in her pocket.

:: sleeper@1 [card:02]
Fog presses at the windows of the sleeper. Curtained berths line the corridor. At the far end, a brass plate on a locked door: S. ARDENT. Colonel Marsh sits up in a quilted gown, reading by lamplight.

{embed nib: 'compartment'}
{embed nib: 'colonel'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: dining@1 [card:03]
The dining car smells of spilled claret. A rolled blueprint lies half under Hobbs’s tray. Mrs. Ardent sits very straight, a sealed letter by her plate.

[if here.has(vell)]
Miss Vell passes through without a word.

[if not cufflink.taken]
Something glints beside the sugar bowl.

[if me.past]
Your echo stands at the bar, exactly where you remember standing. You keep out of its sight.

[if here.passed]
{passers} tore through a moment ago; the cutlery is still rattling.

[end]
{embed nib: 'dining_table'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: lounge@1 [card:04]
Hobbs has laid a tablecloth over the Professor. Mr. Crane hasn’t left the bar. He watches the fog slide past the observation glass and orders another brandy.

{embed nib: 'the_body'}
{embed nib: 'lounge_bar'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: baggage@1 [card:05]
Trunks are strapped to the walls. Behind a brass cage the generator thrums, and your watch hums faintly as you come near. At the rear, the vestibule door rattles in its frame.

{embed nib: 'baggage_car'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: mail@1 [card:06]
moves: walk
--
Mail sacks crowd the aisle; there’s no room to run. By the sorting table sits a crate stencilled FRAGILE — PATENT OFFICE, nailed shut.

{embed nib: 'crate'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: sleeper@2 [card:07]
Rain drums on the roof at Coldwater. Somewhere a door to the platform opens, and closes again.

[if here.asleep(marsh)]
Colonel Marsh’s curtain is drawn; he snores.

[else]
Colonel Marsh is up in his gown, grumbling about the noise.

[if here.has(vell)]
Miss Vell stands at the Professor’s door, trying the handle. She stops when she sees you.

[end]
{embed nib: 'compartment'}
{embed nib: 'colonel'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: dining@2 [card:08]
Rain streaks the windows. Hobbs resets the tables as if nothing has happened. Mrs. Ardent has not touched her soup.

[if not cufflink.taken]
Something still glints beside the sugar bowl.

[end]
{embed nib: 'dining_table'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: lounge@2 [card:09]
At Coldwater two railway policemen look in, see the cloth over the Professor, and are told it can wait for Kingsgate. Mr. Crane signs something for them with a flourish.

{embed nib: 'the_body'}
{embed nib: 'lounge_bar'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: baggage@2 [card:10]
Rain hammers the roof. Through the vestibule glass: the Coldwater platform, empty but for a rain barrel under a lamp.

> [[Watch the platform->baggage@2:platform]] ~ examine ~ when not vell.cornered
{embed nib: 'baggage_car'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: baggage@2:platform [act]
learn coldwater_step
--
A woman in a dark coat bends over the rain barrel at the far end, then hurries back toward the front of the train.

:: mail@2 [card:11]
moves: walk
--
New sacks swing aboard at Coldwater. On the sorting table lies a telegram: PROF. S. ARDENT, NIGHT EXPRESS. Unopened.

{embed nib: 'telegram'}
{embed nib: 'crate'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: sleeper@3 [card:12]
The rain has passed. Moonlight slides along the corridor at Merrow, and the curtains sway.

[if here.asleep(marsh)]
Colonel Marsh snores behind his curtain.

[if here.asleep(vell)]
Miss Vell is curled in a berth, breathing slow and even.

[if not notebook.exists]
Ash in the washbasin, and a blackened brass clasp. Someone has burned a book.

[end]
{embed nib: 'berth'}
{embed nib: 'colonel'}
{embed nib: 'compartment'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: dining@3 [card:13]
Merrow’s single lamp slides past the windows. Hobbs has set out a cold supper no one eats. Mrs. Ardent is writing a second letter.

{embed nib: 'dining_table'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: lounge@3 [card:14]
The staff have carried the Professor to the baggage car. The demonstration table is bare, and Mr. Crane has moved one stool closer to it.

[if not vell_ticket.taken]
Where he lay, a ticket stub catches the lamplight.

[end]
{embed nib: 'ticket'}
{embed nib: 'lounge_bar'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: baggage@3 [card:15]
The generator thrums. The Professor lies under a tarpaulin by the vestibule door, which rattles at every curve.

{embed nib: 'the_body'}
{embed nib: 'baggage_car'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: mail@3 [card:16]
moves: walk
--
Moonlight through the slats. The crate’s label flaps loose: it comes off at Harrow Junction, the next stop.

{embed nib: 'crate'}
{embed nib: 'telegram'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: sleeper@4 [card:17]
A freight train hisses alongside at Harrow Junction, close enough to touch. The corridor shudders. Every curtain is drawn.

[if here.asleep(vell)]
Behind one curtain, Miss Vell breathes slow and even.

[if not notebook.exists]
Ash in the washbasin, and a blackened brass clasp.

[end]
{embed nib: 'berth'}
{embed nib: 'colonel'}
{embed nib: 'compartment'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: dining@4 [card:18]
The freight’s lamps strobe through the dining car. Hobbs steadies the glasses. Mrs. Ardent seals her second letter and asks him for a stamp.

{embed nib: 'dining_table'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: lounge@4 [card:19]
Signal lamps change from red to green. Mr. Crane checks his watch, an ordinary one, against the station clock, and frowns.

[if not vell_ticket.taken]
A ticket stub still lies by the demonstration table.

[end]
{embed nib: 'ticket'}
{embed nib: 'lounge_bar'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: baggage@4 [card:20]
Porters on the Harrow platform shout about the mail. Through the vestibule glass: a freight wagon, and dark fields beyond.

[if here.has(vell) and vell.cornered]
Miss Vell is at the vestibule door, one hand on the latch.

[end]
{embed nib: 'the_body'}
{embed nib: 'baggage_car'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: mail@4 [card:21]
moves: walk
--
Two porters climb aboard for the crate marked PATENT OFFICE. At the end of this stop, it leaves the train.

{embed nib: 'crate'}
{embed nib: 'telegram'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: sleeper@5 [card:22]
Grey light at Fenwick. Colonel Marsh is up, shaving at the basin, braces dangling.

[if not notebook.exists]
Ash in the washbasin, and a blackened brass clasp.

[end]
{embed nib: 'colonel'}
{embed nib: 'compartment'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: dining@5 [card:23]
Hobbs lays breakfast for passengers who will not eat it. Mrs. Ardent asks whether anyone has seen Miss Vell.

[if here.has(vell)]
Miss Vell passes through toward the mail car, gloves on.

[end]
{embed nib: 'dining_table'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: lounge@5 [card:24]
The Fenwick platform clock reads ten to five. Mr. Crane has stopped drinking. “Whoever it was,” he says, “they had better be quick.”

{embed nib: 'ticket'}
{embed nib: 'lounge_bar'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: baggage@5 [card:25]
The generator winds down for the terminus. Someone has left the vestibule door unlatched.

[if here.has(vell) and vell.cornered]
Miss Vell is at the vestibule door, one hand on the latch.

[end]
{embed nib: 'the_body'}
{embed nib: 'baggage_car'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: mail@5 [card:26]
moves: walk
--
The sorting table is bare. Where the crate stood: a chalk mark, or a splintered, empty crate.

{embed nib: 'telegram'}
{embed nib: 'pressure'}

:: terminus [finale card:27]
The night express sighs into Kingsgate at dawn, and {present} step down onto the platform.

[if vell.offstage]
Miss Vell is not among the passengers. At one of the stations, the vestibule door stood open.

[if vell.detained]
Miss Vell walks between two porters, insisting she only wanted air.

[if cohort.alive == cohort.size]
No one is missing. The conductor counts you twice anyway.

[else]
Not everyone stepped down with you, though you feel the missing at your shoulder.

[end]
Deliberate together, then cast your ballots. They are revealed all at once.

{accuse who: suspect, how: scenario.methods, proof: proof_who and proof_how, revote: 1}
> [[Hear the verdict->verdict]] ~ when accusation.done

:: verdict [finale card:28]
[if accusation.proven and not vell.offstage]
At Kingsgate two constables are waiting. Miss Vell holds out her burned hand for the cuffs, as if offering it to be read.

[if accusation.correct and not accusation.proven]
The constables listen, then shrug. Without proof she is free to go, hands in her pockets.

[if accusation.proven and vell.offstage]
A warrant goes out by telegraph from Kingsgate. Somewhere beyond Harrow, a woman with a bandaged hand hears the wires sing.

[if not accusation.correct]
Miss Vell tips her hat to you and is gone into the crowd. That winter the chronometer is patented, under her name.

[end]
“I built it. Every gear, every correction. He put his name on my work and meant to sell it tonight to pay his debts. I only wound his watch past the red mark. He did the rest himself.”
